  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two batteries with e.m.f.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;are connected in parallel across a load resistor of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>. The internal resistance of the two batteries are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively. The voltage across the load lies between,&nbsp;</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
